# The `profile` producer: the image profile marker, as two alternative packages.
#
# Plain `KEY=value` lines only: no logic, no command substitution, no
# expansion. Safe to source from bash and to parse with grep/sed from anything
# else, and checked for that shape by build-env/deb/build.sh before it is
# sourced. build-env/deb/README.md documents every field.

# Two packages, one payload shape. Exactly one of them is installed into an
# image; they Conflict by name and both Provide `mos-profile`.
PACKAGES="mos-profile-dev mos-profile-prod"

# `all` and not `amd64 arm64`. The entire payload is a 17-byte text file and a
# copyright, with no ELF anywhere, so one archive is correct for every image
# this repository builds and building two would be two names for one thing.
ARCHES="all"

# `family` is rootfs/packages-src itself, and it is here for one file: the
# shared copyright. The primary build context is this producer's OWN
# directory, so anything held in common with the sibling producers sits one
# level up and has to be named to be reachable.
# Nothing else is named: this producer's whole payload is written by the
# packing stage from the two profile values, so there is no source tree for it
# to reach into.
BUILD_CONTEXTS="family=rootfs/packages-src"

# Neither package starts anything: the whole payload is one immutable file and
# a copyright, with no unit anywhere in it. The zero is WRITTEN rather than
# omitted because a package that enables nothing and a package nobody counted
# are indistinguishable in a field that is left out.
ENABLEMENT="mos-profile-dev=0 mos-profile-prod=0"
